.TH GTASKS-PANEL 1 "2026-09-10" "gtasks-panel 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gtasks-panel \- Google Tasks counter for the XFCE Generic Monitor plugin
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gtasks-panel
.br
.B gtasks-panel
.B \-\-fetch
.br
.B gtasks-panel
.B \-\-auth
.br
.B gtasks-panel
.B \-\-status
.br
.B gtasks-panel
.B \-\-install\-panel
.RB [ \-\-period
.IR SECONDS ]
.RB [ \-\-panel
.IR N ]
.br
.B gtasks-panel
.B \-\-uninstall\-panel
.br
.B gtasks-panel
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without options,
.B gtasks-panel
prints XML for the xfce4-genmon-plugin with the number of open Google
Tasks across all task lists. Genmon runs it on a timer. A click on the
item runs
.BR gtasks-window (1):
one click opens a popup, two clicks open the full window.
.PP
Genmon blocks the panel while the command runs. So this mode does no
network I/O. It reads the state file and prints it. When the file is
older than
.I refresh
seconds (config.ini, default 300) it starts
.B "gtasks-panel \-\-fetch"
in the background.
.PP
This mode never changes tasks. The sign-in uses the scope
.IR https://www.googleapis.com/auth/tasks ,
because
.BR gtasks-window (1)
shares the same token and does change tasks.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-fetch
Query Google and write the state file. Exits 1 when another fetch runs,
when sign-in is missing, or when the query fails. The error goes to the
state file and to the panel tooltip.
.TP
.B \-\-auth
Sign in with Google. Opens a browser for the OAuth consent. Saves the
token to
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/gtasks-panel/token.json .
Then runs one fetch.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print paths, token state, the last count, and the last error as plain
text.
.TP
.B \-\-install\-panel
Add a Generic Monitor item that runs this script. Inserts it left of the
system tray on panel
.I N
(default 0) with genmon period
.I SECONDS
(default 60, minimum 30). Restarts the panel.
.TP
.B \-\-uninstall\-panel
Remove that item. Restarts the panel.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH PANEL STATES
.TP
.I number
Open tasks.
.TP
.I number?
Last known count. The last refresh failed. See the tooltip.
.TP
.B \&...
No count yet. A fetch runs, or the first fetch failed. See the tooltip.
.TP
.B setup
No OAuth client file. Click to open the window. It shows where to put
the file.
.TP
.B "sign in"
No token, or the token expired, or it was revoked, or it does not have
the read-write scope that version 0.2.0 needs. Click to sign in.
.TP
.B !
The script crashed. See the tooltip.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gtasks-panel/client_secret.json
OAuth client from Google Cloud Console (Desktop app). You add it.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gtasks-panel/config.ini
Optional settings: icon, icon_overdue, label, open_command, refresh,
default_list.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/gtasks-panel/token.json
Saved sign-in.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/gtasks-panel/state.json
Last count, last error, sign-in state.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/gtasks-panel/lock
Held while a fetch runs.
.SH NOTES
An OAuth app in "Testing" status gives tokens that expire after 7 days.
Set the consent screen to "In production" for a long-lived token.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gtasks-window (1),
.BR xfce4-panel (1)
